Package: evtests
Title: Tests and Diagnostics for the Upper Tail of a Distribution
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Rodrigo Fonseca", "Villa", email = "rodrigo03.villa@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0005-2938-2270"))
Description: Semiparametric tools to examine the upper tail of a sample before
    an extreme value analysis: tests of the extreme value condition, tests of
    the domain of attraction and of a finite end-point, estimators of the
    extreme value index and of the end-point, and the choice of the number of
    upper order statistics. Includes the tests of Hasofer and Wang (1992),
    Segers and Teugels (2000), Dietrich, de Haan and Husler (2002), Neves,
    Picek and Fraga Alves (2006), Drees, de Haan and Li (2006), Neves and
    Fraga Alves (2007), Neves and Pereira (2010), del Castillo, Daoudi and
    Lockhart (2014) and Fraga Alves, Neves and Rosario (2016), and the
    goodness-of-fit tests of Choulakian and Stephens (2001). Each method is
    tested against the numerical results of its source paper, and the
    differences found are documented.
